# The Pieces of a FastAPI Route

```python
@app.get("/")
def read_root():
    return {"Hello": "World"}
```

- `@app.get("/")` is a **decorator** that tells FastAPI this function handles GET requests to the root path.
- The function name is arbitrary but descriptive.
- The return value is automatically converted to JSON.

You can also use `@app.post()`, `@app.put()`, `@app.delete()`, etc.
